 **Goal:** Build the headless, deterministic falling-block engine in `internal/game`: pieces, board, 7-bag, movement, wall kicks, gravity, lock delay, line clearing, hold, scoring, and game over, with no rendering and no clock reads.
 
-**Architecture:** One Go package, `internal/game`, holding plain structs and pure-ish functions. `Game` owns all mutable state plus its own `*rand.Rand`. Two entry points drive it: `Apply(Input)` for player actions and `Tick(dt)` for elapsed time. Both return `[]Event`, which is the engine's only outbound channel — later plans (renderer, FX) consume events and never reach into state. Nothing in this package imports Bubble Tea, Lip Gloss, or `time.Now()`.
